00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:29.000
He liked tinkering with things, he built little toys. This is Tompazek. He works at the Bundy Museum, which, as you can imagine, is all about Willard Bundy. As a child, he would like take apart watches and try to reassemble them. Willard grew up to become a professional watchtinkerer, a jeweler, because back then, jewelers weren't just jewelers. They were the town's authority on time. It was their responsibility to build these big, accurate clocks and keep them on display in their shop window so that people
可以去橱窗看看现在几点。而这份工作中威拉德最喜欢的就是这一部分。他会花上数小时甚至数天来构建这些复杂的创意时钟，比如这个他声称可以保持一千年精准时间的八英尺高的庞然大物。它不仅有显示时、分、秒的表盘，还有星期、日期、月份以及未来一千年的年份。但这个时钟，顺便说一下，他称之为“奇妙时钟”，不仅仅是为了报时。它还有每小时都会鸣响的铃铛和哨子。

