00:04:29.000 --> 00:05:13.000
could visit the window and see what time it was. And it was this part of the job that Willard loved the most. He'd spent hours and hours constructing these intricate novelty clocks, like this hulking eight-foot-tall clock that he claimed could keep perfect time for a thousand years. It had dials for not only hours, minutes, and seconds, but also the day of the week, the date of the month, which particular month it was, and the year for 1,000 years. But this clock, which, by the way, he called the wonderful clock, wasn't, just for telling time. It had bells and whistles that would chime on the hour, every hour.
这东西本质上就是一个加强版的布谷鸟钟。但威拉德没有让鸟儿跳出来，而是构建了一个精致的场景，一种工作磨坊的机械立体模型。我想那实际上是一个木材加工厂，所以瀑布在运输小木头去切割。还有一个带有青蛙、乌龟和各种鱼类的小池塘。有一个微型蒸汽机和一条在池塘里漂浮的小船。这个时钟太受欢迎了，太奇特了，

