00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:32.000
that he saw the messiness of timekeeping happening in factories across America as a giant problem he needed to solve. The story goes that one day, Willard walked into a factory in his town and saw how the bosses were keeping track of their employees' time. They assigned each worker one of these little brass discs and expected them to toss it into a bucket every morning to mark themselves present. But the system was a mess. It was sloppy.
没有关于工人实际到达时间的准确记录。威拉德无法控制自己。他看到了一个现存的系统，但它不够好。于是回到店里，威拉德开始制造一些足够好的东西。1888年，他申请了专利，这就是第一台员工考勤钟——邦迪时钟。它基本上是一个挂在墙上的华丽木箱，有点像落地钟。除了钟面下方有一个插钥匙的小槽。每个工人都有自己的钥匙。

