00:06:32.000 --> 00:07:04.000
There was no accurate record of when the guy actually showed up. And Willard, he couldn't help himself. He saw a system that existed, but it wasn't up to snuff. So back in his shop, Willard started building something that was up to snuff. And in 1888, he patented it, the first employee time clock, the Bundy clock. It was basically an ornate wooden box mounted on the wall, kind of like a grandfather clock. Except underneath the clock face, there was a little slot for a key. Each worker got their own key.
每天早上，当他们来上班时，他们会把钥匙插入槽中，转动四分之一圈，这就会在纸带上印下他们到达的确切时间。但在申请专利后，威拉德对销售它的想法并不太感兴趣。我想威拉德满足于守住自己的本分。他想制造那些带给他快乐的特定物品。他并不一定想发财。他并没有试图重新定义这个系统。也许威拉德不想发财，但他的兄弟想。

