And every morning, when they showed up to work, they'd insert their key into the slot. turn it a quarter turn, which would then stamp the exact time they got there onto a ribbon of paper. But after he patented it, Willard wasn't really that into the idea of selling it. Willard was content to stay in his lane, I guess. He wanted to make these very specific objects that brought him joy. He wasn't necessarily looking to get rich. He wasn't trying to redefine the system. Maybe Willard wasn't trying to get rich, but his brother was,
威拉德的弟弟哈洛将在邦迪时钟的故事中扮演重要角色。但哈洛想要威拉德不想要的东西。事实上，邦迪兄弟俩的性格截然不同。很明显，我们这位博物馆的讲解员有偏爱。我们所知道的关于威拉德的一切都告诉我们，他是一个真正的好人。他在社区里很受欢迎。他的弟弟哈洛则完全相反。他粗鲁。

