He was aware of what his brother was inventing. He said, hey, if we market these clocks, they're going to sell like hot cakes. Eventually, Harlow convinces his inventor brother to go into business with him. But the Bundy clocks do not immediately sell, like hotcakes. A lot of business owners didn't necessarily see the need for a time clock like this. Plus, this clock was expensive. A Bundy clock was $75, which I want to say that calculates to about $1,500 to $2,000. The other problem was that for the first year, they tried to market these clocks directly to workers.
他们会在工会杂志或工厂城镇的报纸上刊登广告，上面写着：“嘿，工厂工人，确保你的老板付给你的工资是正确的，鼓励他买一台邦迪时钟。”但这个策略结果是一个巨大的失败。如果你的想法是让所有的同事都团结在这个设备周围，并告诉你的老板去买它，他们是不会这么做的。你知道，他们会做那些能为自己省钱的事。老板们根本不会听工人的。所以很快他们就放弃了这个想法。公司里的某个人想出了一个天才的主意，改变了策略。

