They would take out ads in union magazines or newspapers in factory towns that would read, Hey, factory worker, make sure your boss is paying you correctly, encourage him to buy a Bundy clock. But this strategy turned out to be a big old flop. If the idea was you get all of your coworkers to rally around this device and tell your boss to buy it, they're not going to do it. You know, they're going to do what saves them money. The bosses weren't going to listen to their workers. So pretty soon they dump that idea. Someone at the company has the genius idea of flipping the script.
他们刊登了广告，上面写着：“嘿，工厂主们。确保你没有被懒惰、不诚实的工人欺骗。买一台邦迪时钟，追踪他们的工时。”叮，叮，叮。说中了。然后，他们开始热销。我们不确定是哪个兄弟想出了这个主意。但在汤姆看来，这很典型是哈洛的风格。

